nts:\n\n- $4000 \\leq N < 6000$ (starting digit 4 or 5)\n- $N \\equiv 0 \\pmod{5}$ (ending digit 0)\n- $3 \\leq b < c \\leq 6$\n\nWe already know there are 9 combinations for $(b, c)$ that meet the pairwise inequality constraints.\n\nHence, the final count of such numbers is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{9}\n\\]",
